menu "espOS SignalK"

    config ESPOS_SK_RX_FRAME_MAX
        int "Largest inbound stream frame kept (bytes)"
        default 16384
        range 2048 131072
        help
            Delta messages larger than this are dropped (logged). A
            subscription burst after reconnect (values + meta for many
            paths) can reach several KiB; raise on PSRAM boards that
            subscribe to whole families.

    config ESPOS_SK_NOTIFICATIONS
        bool "Device-health notifications"
        default y
        help
            Publish espos_health conditions as SignalK notifications
            under notifications.espos.<label>.<key> -- memory pressure, a
            dependency that has gone away, whatever the application
            reports.

            Without them such a condition surfaces as a device that has
            quietly stopped working, which looks the same as a hardware
            fault and is the expensive kind of problem to diagnose.

            Turning it off drops the sink and the periodic low-memory
            check; conditions are still recorded by espos_health and still
            reach any other sink. The number of distinct conditions is
            ESPOS_HEALTH_MAX_CONDITIONS, under "espOS health".

endmenu
